# Docs follow the code

If you change behavior, layout, or a public claim, update the pages in the table. Skip docs only for refactors that do not change any claim a reader could quote (rename a private helper, comment-only).

Public site is `docs/` (MkDocs). Engineer notes are `notes/` and the root `README.md`. The attack table lives only in `docs/security.md`.

Day numbers belong in `roadmap.md`, not in code comments, `docs/`, or `notes/`.

## Map (edit → open)

| You changed | Update these |
| --- | --- |
| `programs/**/settle*` / vault spend / SPL legs | `docs/solana-program.md`, `docs/architecture.md` phase D |
| `programs/**/state.rs`, sizes, seeds, padding | `docs/solana-program.md` table, `notes/budgets.md`, `notes/layout-signer-audit.md` |
| Pause, admin, `has_one`, root register | `docs/security.md`, glossary **protocol admin** |
| Journal / `PublicOutputs` / Poseidon / guest rules | `docs/circuit.md`, `docs/tests.md` happy journal, `docs/glossary.md` ZK terms |
| Fixtures, vkey, prove path | `docs/circuit.md` fixtures, `notes/proving.md`, `zk-circuit/fixtures/happy/README.md` |
| Relayer, 402, fee payer | `docs/architecture.md` phase E, `docs/security.md` A16, `notes/relayer-economics.md` |
| SDK / UI submit path | `docs/architecture.md` phase A, `docs/index.md` status, `ui/README.md` |
| Compute units / ix byte size | `notes/budgets.md`, root README measured-cost table |
| Roadmap rank / “next Day” | `roadmap.md` calendar **and** `docs/index.md` status row (no Day numbers in `docs/`) |

## How to decide

1. Name the **user-visible claim** you changed (e.g. “settle still debit the user’s mint A”).
2. Grep `docs/` and `notes/` for that claim (old SPL legs, “upcoming” vault-only, “planned” root register).
3. Fix every hit so shipped vs upcoming matches `roadmap.md`. Prefer one sentence over a new page.
4. If a threat-model ID (A01–A25) is involved, edit `docs/security.md` only.

## Do not

- Leave `docs/` saying wallet→vault settle if the program is vault-only
- Mark a feature “planned” after its Day Exit is `[x]`
- Duplicate the A01–A25 table into the README
- Put `Day N` in code comments or public docs
